---
import Base from "@layouts/Base.astro";
import { brand } from "../brand/config";

// Locked brand values for legal copy.
const T = {
  name: brand.name,
  legal: brand.legalName,
  short: brand.shortName,
  year: new Date().getFullYear(),
  docVersion: "0.9.0-draft",
  effectiveOn: "TBD — pending Australian legal review",
};
---

<Base
  title="Terms"
  description={`Plain-language terms and the formal ${brand.name} membership agreement.`}
  canonicalPath="/terms/"
>
  <section class="pwy-page pwy-legal" aria-labelledby="terms-heading">
    <div class="pwy-shell">
      <header class="pwy-legal__head">
        <p class="pwy-kicker">The arrangement / terms</p>
        <h1 id="terms-heading">Terms</h1>
        <p class="pwy-legal__lead">
          The waitlist is free and does not create paid membership. Paid membership and payment are
          currently closed. This page is a plain-language draft while the formal agreement is
          finalised with Australian-facing legal review.
        </p>
        <p class="pwy-legal__status"><strong>Draft v{T.docVersion}</strong> · {T.effectiveOn}</p>
      </header>

      <h2>Plain-language summary</h2>
      <p>By joining {T.short}, you agree to the following in plain language:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          You will receive invitations to <strong>constructed ordinary events</strong>. These events
          are not real in the way a conference or a wedding is real. They are constructed by {
            T.short
          } on purpose.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Ordinary events are intended to be cancelled</strong> before the date. A completely
          silent member is a successful member. We will never charge a per-event surcharge.
        </li>
        <li>
          Some <strong
            >characters, locations, and references in our correspondence are fictional</strong
          >. We do not claim fictional people, places, or partnerships as real.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>AI and automation assist personalisation</strong> within the rules we set. A human operator
          reviews selected outputs and performs real-world tasks (print, sign, post, call, gift).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Optional services are controllable</strong>. The default for every optional
          service is off. You can opt in, opt out, and revoke already-scheduled future work for any
          service.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>You can leave at any time</strong>. Cancellation stops future personalisation and
          any already-scheduled work for the cancelled services. Required records (e.g. financial
          records) are kept for the minimum period required by law.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Formal membership agreement</h2>
      <p>
        This section is the formal agreement between you and {T.legal} ("we", "us", "{T.short}").
        The plain-language summary above is provided for clarity and is not the agreement.
      </p>

      <h3>1. Membership</h3>
      <p>
        1.1 {T.legal} operates a tiered membership program with three tiers: Member, Corresponding Member,
        and Deluxe Member. Pricing is per individual, per month, in Australian dollars. Tier capabilities
        are described on the <a href="/membership/">membership page</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        1.2 Membership is a month-to-month recurring subscription. We do not require an annual
        contract. You may cancel at any time; cancellation takes effect at the end of the current
        billing period and stops future personalisation.
      </p>
      <p>
        1.3 Paid activation is not available at the current waitlist launch. When billing is
        enabled, activation will require: (a) completion of identity verification; (b) acceptance of
        the current terms and privacy policy; (c) successful billing authorisation via the enabled
        billing provider; and (d) an activation confirmation recorded against your member record.
        Joining the waitlist satisfies none of these gates and collects no payment.
      </p>

      <h3>2. Constructed ordinary events</h3>
      <p>
        2.1 {T.short} will, from time to time, send you invitations to ordinary events. The cadence is
        set by your preferences (occasional, about monthly, a couple per month, or "use our discretion").
        Cadence is honoured approximately, not exactly.
      </p>
      <p>
        2.2 Ordinary events are <strong>constructed</strong> — that is, created by {T.short} on purpose.
        They are not real social, cultural, or commercial events of the kind advertised by a venue or
        a business. Locations referenced in invitations are real public addresses, but the events themselves
        are not real events at those addresses.
      </p>
      <p>
        2.3 {T.short} intends to cancel every ordinary event before its scheduled start. The default cancellation
        window is 12 to 36 hours before the event; some cancellations land earlier ("merciful") and some
        later ("last minute"). {T.short} will not cancel an event after it has begun.
      </p>
      <p>
        2.4 Cancellation is successful fulfilment, not failure. You are not expected to attend. A
        completely silent member is a successful member.
      </p>

      <h3>3. Fictional references</h3>
      <p>
        3.1 {T.short} correspondence may mention characters, locations, and references that are fictional.
        Real public addresses may be used as scene locations, but the events at those addresses are constructed
        by {T.short} and are not real events.
      </p>
      <p>
        3.2 {T.short} will not claim fictional characters, locations, or partnerships as real people,
        places, or commercial partners. If a real third party is referenced (e.g. a real public café as
        a scene location), {T.short} will not represent that third party as endorsing, sponsoring, or
        hosting the constructed event.
      </p>

      <h3>4. Optional services</h3>
      <p>
        4.1 Optional services include: posted correspondence, gifts, calls, manufactured
        commitments, and the real-world appearance service. Each optional service is an explicit
        opt-in. The default for every optional service is off.
      </p>
      <p>
        4.2 You may opt in or opt out of any optional service at any time. Opting out of a service
        pauses that service and cancels any already-scheduled future work for that service. Other
        membership actions continue unaffected.
      </p>
      <p>
        4.3 The real-world appearance service is a separate paid service, not bundled with any tier.
        Travel and substantial preparation are quoted separately. {T.short} will not provide a representative
        for any purpose involving impersonation of real authorities, fraud, harassment, or illegal activity.
      </p>

      <h3>5. Personalisation consent and memory</h3>
      <p>
        5.1 {T.short} will use the confirmed facts you have shared, plus your stated preferences, to personalise
        correspondence. You may view, edit, or remove any confirmed fact at any time from the member portal.
        You may mark any fact as "do not mention" and
        {T.short} will respect that.
      </p>
      <p>
        5.2 {T.short} will not infer sensitive personal categories for personalisation. {T.short}
        will not use your data to train general AI models. {T.short} will not sell your data or share
        it with third parties except as required to deliver the service.
      </p>
      <p>
        5.3 AI may propose candidate facts (e.g. a fact inferred from an inbound message). Candidate
        facts are stored separately and require your explicit confirmation before they are used in
        correspondence. {T.short} will not invent facts about you.
      </p>

      <h3>6. Physical fulfilment consent</h3>
      <p>
        6.1 Posted correspondence and physical artefacts will only be sent to the postal address on
        your member record. Surprise packages are sent only if you have explicitly opted in to them.
      </p>
      <p>
        6.2 {T.short} sets real, transparent budget limits on physical fulfilment. Budgets are described
        on the <a href="/membership/">membership page</a>. {T.short} will not independently make expensive
        purchases; operator approval is required for any purchase above the published per-item threshold.
      </p>

      <h3>7. Call consent</h3>
      <p>
        7.1 Calls require explicit opt-in. The default is no calls. When calls are enabled,
        {T.short} will only call within the window you have specified. Voicemail is used only if you have
        explicitly opted in to it.
      </p>
      <p>
        7.2 Calls are scripted and reviewed for do-not-mention compliance. The caller identifies as
        calling from {T.short} and will not impersonate a third party.
      </p>

      <h3>8. Manufactured commitments</h3>
      <p>
        8.1 A manufactured commitment is a consensual artificial social obligation. You may ask {
          T.short
        } to construct a plausible scenario, confirm it, and use it to create useful pressure toward a
        goal you have set. {T.short} will then explicitly cancel the scenario.
      </p>
      <p>
        8.2 You may abort a manufactured commitment at any time. Aborting cancels the scenario and
        clears future reminders. Nothing dangles.
      </p>

      <h3>9. Cancellation, refunds, and termination</h3>
      <p>
        9.1 You may cancel your membership at any time from the member portal. Cancellation stops
        future personalisation and any already-scheduled work for the cancelled services.
        Cancellation is effective at the end of the current billing period.
      </p>
      <p>
        9.2 Refunds for the current billing period are at our discretion. We do not charge
        per-event, per-RSVP, or per-cancellation, so there is no per-event refund pathway.
      </p>
      <p>
        9.3 We may suspend or terminate a membership that materially breaches these terms, including
        (a) abusive conduct toward operators, (b) fraudulent use of optional services, or (c) use of
        the appearance service for prohibited purposes.
      </p>

      <h3>10. Privacy and data</h3>
      <p>
        10.1 Your data is handled under the published <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>, which
        forms part of these terms.
      </p>
      <p>
        10.2 Account deletion stops future personalisation and triggers the data-removal workflow.
        Required records (e.g. financial records) are kept for the minimum period required by law
        and then removed.
      </p>

      <h3>11. Limitation of liability</h3>
      <p>
        11.1 To the extent permitted by law, our liability is limited to the amount you have paid us
        in the 12 months preceding the claim. We are not liable for indirect, incidental, or
        consequential damages.
      </p>
      <p>
        11.2 Nothing in these terms excludes, restricts, or modifies any guarantee, condition, or
        warranty that cannot be excluded under the Australian Consumer Law.
      </p>

      <h3>12. Changes to these terms</h3>
      <p>
        12.1 We may update these terms from time to time. The current version, effective date, and
        content hash are always published on this page. We will notify you by email of any material
        change.
      </p>
      <p>
        12.2 Re-acceptance of an updated document does not by itself re-charge or change your
        membership. If you do not agree to an updated version, you may cancel.
      </p>

      <h3>13. Governing law</h3>
      <p>
        13.1 These terms are governed by the laws of Victoria, Australia. The parties submit to the
        non-exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of Victoria.
      </p>

      <h3>14. Contact</h3>
      <p>
        14.1 Questions about these terms: <a href="/waiting-list/">join the waiting list</a>
        and write to us, or reply to any {T.short} email.
      </p>

      <h2>Document version</h2>
      <p class="pwy-legal__version">
        Version: {T.docVersion} · Effective: {T.effectiveOn}<br />
        © {T.year}
        {T.legal}
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .pwy-page {
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .pwy-shell {
    max-width: 78rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 clamp(1rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }
  .pwy-legal {
    padding: clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 6rem) 0 5rem;
  }
  .pwy-legal__head {
    padding-bottom: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .pwy-kicker {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--fg-faint);
    font: 600 0.72rem/1.2 var(--font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .pwy-legal h1 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font: 400 clamp(3.5rem, 10vw, 8rem)/0.84 var(--font-serif);
    letter-spacing: -0.06em;
  }
  .pwy-legal__lead {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 1.8vw, 1.35rem);
  }
  .pwy-legal__status {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    color: var(--accent);
    font: 0.75rem/1.4 var(--font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  .pwy-legal > .pwy-shell > h2 {
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem);
  }
  .pwy-legal h2 {
    font: 400 clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.8rem)/1 var(--font-serif);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }
  .pwy-legal h3 {
    margin-top: 2.2rem;
    font: 400 1.4rem/1.1 var(--font-serif);
  }
  .pwy-legal p,
  .pwy-legal li {
    max-width: 48rem;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }
  .pwy-legal li {
    margin: 0.7rem 0;
  }
  .pwy-legal strong {
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .pwy-legal__version {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--fg-faint) !important;
    font: 0.75rem/1.6 var(--font-mono);
  }
</style>
